{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/2/context.json","@type":"sc:Manifest","@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/p16003coll14:1503/manifest.json","label":"Astrological and medical compilation, end of the 15th century","metadata":[{"label":"Administrative Notes","value":"Manuscripts"},{"label":"Call Number","value":"mssHM 64"},{"label":"Catalog Link","value":"https://catalog.huntington.org/record=b1841462"},{"label":"Contributor","value":"John XXI, Pope, -1277. ; Johannes Paulinus. ; Galen. ; Joannes Jacobi, -1384. ; Hippocrates."},{"label":"Date Searchable","value":"1485-1499"},{"label":"Date","value":"1485-1499"},{"label":"Digital Collection","value":"History of Science, Technology, and Medicine"},{"label":"Form/Genre","value":"Manuscripts England 15th century. (aat)"},{"label":"Language","value":"Latin [lat] ; English [eng] ; French [fre]"},{"label":"Notes","value":"Ms. codex. Compilation of several astrological and medical works, including a calendar, astronomical and astrological tables, medical recipes and charms. Title from printed catalogue. Paper,  i + 196 + i; 1²⁴ (as suggested by paired presence and absence of watermarks, - the first 2 leaves and the last leaf, after f. 29; + an inserted gathering of 8 leaves, ff. 18-25) 2²⁶(-10 after f. 38) 3²² 4-8²⁴.  2 catchwords only, at the end of quire 2 (f. 54v) and quire 8 (f. 196v), both enclosed in red frames. 2 columns of 32-37 lines, except on ff. 34v-47v (arts. 21, 22) with long lines, and ff. 72v-79 (art. 30) in verse. Ruled in lead; round prick marks in the 3 outer margins. Contemporary foliation shows loss of one leaf after f. 29 and after the present f. 38, both with loss of text; the foliation apparently skipped the numbers 44 and 88, as text and quire structure run continuously. Written in England towards the end of the fifteenth century; computistic cycles in the calendar are dated 1480 and 1520; some of the feasts in the liturgical calendar were instituted in 1480 (Visitation, Frideswide, Etheldreda); the feast of the Transfiguration was instituted in England in 1487; on f. 72 is a mention of Henry VII, showing that part of the text to be written in 1485 or later. Written in a mixed, predominantly secretary script; rubrics usually in a textura formata script; occasional words written in cipher (e.g. ff. 50, 102v, 111, 143, 163). Illustrations in ink, with hair tinted yellow, of a Vein Man (f. 8v) and 2 Zodiac Men (ff. 12v, 14); urine bottles, not colored in, on ff. 39-47v; diagrams, charts, tables and astrological signs in ink of the text, in red and in yellow wash. 4- to 1-line initials, usually in red only, some in red with crude ink flourishing, some also with a yellow wash (through f. 17); 1-line initials in the text slashed in red; red paragraph marks and some red rubrics. Binding: bound in 1971 in polished calf; previous binding, in 18th century English calf."},{"label":"Physical Description","value":"196 leaves : paper ; 307 x 215 (227 x 180) mm."},{"label":"Provenance","value":"Names of early owners are: late 15th century or early 16th century: ff. 82v, 106, 109, 120, 140, 149, “Iste liber est [or “constat”] Iohannis eccam [or “ekam”]”; f. 41, possibly in the same hand as “Iohannis eccam,” “Caucio Iohannis p’ener alias halpyn pro vi s.”; f. 11, “Iohn Han[?]”; early 16th c.: f. 155, “Iohn wallton”; 16th century: f. 196v, “Hughe drapere merchaunt”; 16th century: ff. 74, 76v, 81, 160v, “Iohn Bosgrove” (on f. 81, “Iohn Bosgrove ys a mytte man and man of the lerneing wythall”).  Bought ca. 1833 by Sir Thomas Phillipps; his MS 6883. Acquired privately through A. S. W. Rosenbach by Henry E. Huntington in 1923. "},{"label":"Restrictions","value":"RESTRICTED. Available with curatorial approval. For information on using Huntington Library materials, please see Reproductions of Huntington Library Holdings: http://www.huntington.org/WebAssets/Templates/content.aspx?id=588 . "},{"label":"Rights","value":"For information on use of Digital Library materials, please see Library Rights and Permissions: https://www.huntington.org/library-rights-permissions"},{"label":"Subjects","value":"Astrology -- Early works to 1800. ; Medicine -- Early works to 1800."},{"label":"Title","value":"Astrological and medical compilation, end of the 15th century"},{"label":"Repository","value":"Huntington Digital Library"},{"label":"Source","value":"<span>From: <a href=\"https://hdl.huntington.org/digital/collection/p16003coll14/id/1503\">Astrological and medical compilation, end of the 15th century</a></span>"}],"attribution":["","For information on use of Digital Library materials, please see Library Rights and Permissions: https://www.huntington.org/library-rights-permissions"],"seeAlso":{"@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/oai/oai.php?verb=GetRecord&identifier=oai:cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org:p16003coll14/1503&metadataPrefix=oai_qdc","format":"application/xml","profile":"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/OAI-PMH.xsd"},"within":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/p16003coll14/manifest.json","sequences":[{"@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/p16003coll14:1503/sequence/s0","@type":"sc:Sequence","label":"Astrological and medical compilation, end of the 15th century","canvases":[{"@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/p16003coll14:1102/canvas/c0","@type":"sc:Canvas","label":"Front cover","images":[{"@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/p16003coll14:1102/annotation/a0","@type":"oa:Annotation","motivation":"sc:painting","resource":{"@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/2/p16003coll14:1102/full/full/0/default.jpg","@type":"dctypes:Image","service":{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json","@id":"https://cdm16003.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/2/p16003coll14:1102","width":5782,"height":7200,"tiles":[{"width":5782,"scaleFactors":[1,2,4,8,16]}],"profile":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/level1.json","protocol":"http://iiif.io/api/image"},"format":"image/jpeg","width":5782,"height":7200},"o